# Typography: Kerning true (the default) and false on large titles, where the pairs AV, To and Wa show.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Typography · Kerning
	Page:
		Paper: A4
		Margin: 20mm
	Styles:
		For style: title
			Box:
				Margin: 0 0 16 0
			Typography:
				Size: 40
				Line height: 48
				Bold: true
	Section:
		Text: Typography
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: Kerning
		Paragraph: Some pairs of letters leave a visible gap because of their shape. The engine applies the kerning pairs of the font, which bring them closer, and `Kerning: false` turns them off. It shows in large titles. IBM Plex Mono, where every letter measures the same, has none.
			Style: intro
		Text: Kerning: true  (the default)
			Style: label
		Text: AVATAR · Torre · Wave
			Style: title
		Text: Kerning: false
